---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Admission">
	<h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-900">Admission in Germany</h1>
	<p class="mt-2 text-slate-600">Everything you need to know before you apply — general requirements, Bachelor's eligibility, and Master's eligibility.</p>

	<!-- General overview -->
	<section class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-8 shadow-sm">
		<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">General Overview</h2>
		<p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
			Germany is one of the most popular study destinations in the world, and every year thousands
			of Pakistani students make the move to continue their education there. The two most common
			paths are <strong>Bachelor's</strong> and <strong>Master's</strong> programs — each with its
			own eligibility rules, which we've broken down below.
		</p>
		<p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
			Whichever path fits you, German universities are known for extremely low or even
			<strong> zero tuition fees</strong> at public institutions, strong ties to industry, and
			degrees that are respected internationally — which is exactly why it's become such a
			practical, sought-after choice for building both an education and a career.
		</p>
	</section>

	<!-- Bachelors -->
	<section class="mt-6 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-8 shadow-sm">
		<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Bachelor's Admission</h2>
		<p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
			To be eligible for a Bachelor's program in Germany, you need <strong>13 years of prior
			education</strong>. In Pakistan, students typically complete only <strong>12 years </strong>
			by the time they finish HSSC or A-Levels — which means most Pakistani students are one year
			short of the German requirement.
		</p>
		<p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
			The good news: this gap is easy to close. Take admission into any Bachelor's degree program
			in Pakistan and complete its <strong>first two semesters</strong> (i.e. your first year). At
			that point, you've completed 13 years of education in total and become eligible to apply for
			a Bachelor's program in Germany.
		</p>
		<div class="mt-6 rounded-lg border border-indigo-100 bg-indigo-50 p-4 text-sm text-indigo-800">
			<strong>Example:</strong> You enroll in a 4-year Bachelor's program in Pakistan. After
			finishing just the first 2 semesters, you now meet Germany's 13-year requirement and can
			begin your German university application.
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- Masters -->
	<section class="mt-6 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-8 shadow-sm">
		<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Master's Admission</h2>
		<p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
			For a Master's program in Germany, the requirement steps up to <strong>16 years of
			education</strong> in total.
		</p>
		<p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
			Germany also recognizes the <strong>2+2 year Bachelor's structure</strong> used in some
			systems — so as long as your combined years of education add up to 16, you meet the
			eligibility requirement for a Master's application.
		</p>
	</section>
</Layout>